  "period_note": "Solo (standalone, not consolidated) basis throughout, per project standing rule. RESTATEMENT FOUND: FY2022's own report's comparative column for FY2021 shows Total Provision (D)=414,732,871 (vs this report's own 401,604,033), PBT=1,202,397,262 (vs 1,215,526,100) and PAT=673,218,462 (vs 686,345,431) - a ~13.13m (1.9%) difference, traced exactly to the 'Provision for Start-up Fund' line: this report's own P&L nets a -13,128,837 Start-up Fund credit inside Total Provision (D), reducing it and inflating PBT/PAT; FY2022's report instead excludes this item from the Provision section of the P&L entirely (moving it to a post-tax appropriation, where this report already separately shows a similar-sized Start-up Fund appropriation elsewhere). FY2022 also shows FY2021 EPS as 0.63 (vs this report's own 0.67). Per project standing rule, the contemporaneous FY2021 figures (Total Provision 401,604,033; PBT 1,215,526,100; PAT 686,345,431; EPS 0.67) are used here, not FY2022's restated comparative. General Provision for Unclassified Investments fell to nil this year (from 1,282m in FY2020) - the first year of a multi-year pattern of no unclassified-investment general provisioning that persists through FY2023 (see FY2022/FY2023 notes), coinciding with Bangladesh Bank granting a provision-shortfall deferral (see FY2021 Pillar-3 note: 'General Provision Shortfall of Tk.148.30 crore against Investments... deferred... to be built up equally in next 3 years'). Terminology fully converts to Islamic vocabulary this year: Balance Sheet's main financing line becomes pure 'INVESTMENTS' (previously the dual label 'Loans, Cash Credits, Overdraft etc./ Investments' used FY2011-2020); the credit-quality disclosure becomes 'Statement of Non-Performing Investment' (previously 'Statement of Non-Performing Loan' through the FY2020 report) - this is the exact year the terminology shift documented at the top of sources.json takes effect.",
